-- title:
--   Frobenius-semilinear transport of differentials on q-expansion function fields
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $p$, let $\Gamma\le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ have finite index and contain $T$, and let $F=$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) be the intermediate field of $K((q))/K$ generated by the set of quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_g$, where $f,g$ run over modular forms of a common weight $k$ for $\Gamma$ (viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$) admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ with $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_g\ne 0$. Then there exists an additive endomorphism $\sigma_\Omega$ of $\Omega[F/K]$ with the following three properties. First, $\sigma_\Omega$ is $p$-semilinear over $K$: $\sigma_\Omega(a\cdot\omega)=a^p\cdot\sigma_\Omega\omega$ for all $a\in K$. Second, writing $\Theta=$ [`ModularCurve.diffQExp`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeDifferential.html#L128) for the $F$-linear map $\Omega[F/K]\to K((q))$ obtained by lifting the derivation $q\,d/dq$ restricted to $F$, one has $(\Theta(\sigma_\Omega\omega))_n=((\Theta\omega)_n)^p$ for every $\omega$ and every $n\in\mathbb Z$. Third, for every place $v$ of $F$ over $K$ (a valuation subring $\mathcal O_v\subsetneq F$ containing the image of $K$ and being a principal ideal ring), with $t_v$ the chosen uniformizer of $\mathcal O_v$ and $dt_v$ its differential, and for every $\omega$: if $\omega=f\cdot dt_v$ with $f\in\mathcal O_v$ then $\sigma_\Omega\omega$ is likewise of that shape at the place [`ModularCurve.qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL K Γ p v`](def/ModularCurve_QExpFrobeniusModL.html#L132), the restriction of $v$ along the integral $K$-algebra endomorphism [`ModularCurve.qExpFrobeniusModL K Γ p`](def/ModularCurve_QExpFrobeniusModL.html#L76) of $F$ substituting $q^p$ for $q$; if $\omega=f\cdot dt_v$ with $t_vf\in\mathcal O_v$ (a simple pole) then the same holds for $\sigma_\Omega\omega$ at that place; and if moreover the residue of $t_vf$ equals the image of $r\in K$, then at that place $\sigma_\Omega\omega$ has simple residue $r^p$.
--
--   This is the arithmetic Frobenius transport on the differentials of the $q$-expansion function field of $X(\Gamma)$ in characteristic $p$: coefficientwise $p$-th power on $q$-expansions of differentials, combined with the move of each place to its Frobenius image, and $r\mapsto r^p$ on simple residues. It is used in the residue computation [`ModularCurve.hasSimpleResidue_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_of_isFrobPushDiff`](thm.html#ModularCurve.hasSimpleResidue_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_of_isFrobPushDiff) and its pole-order companion.
